1 PURGE

   Deletes all but the newest versions of files on a mounted volume.

   Format

     PURGE [filespec]

2 Parameter

 filespec

   The files to purge.  Wildcards are allowed.  A version given is
   ignored: PURGE looks at every version of each name it matches.  The
   parts left out are the default device and directory's (see SET
   DEFAULT), and with no filespec PURGE purges *.*, every file in the
   default directory.  Finding no file isn't an error.

2 Qualifiers
/LIMIT=n

   How many of each file's newest versions to keep.  The default is 1,
   the newest alone.

2 Examples

   1.$ PURGE FOO.TXT

     Deletes every version of FOO.TXT but the newest.

   2.$ PURGE/LIMIT=2

     Keeps the two newest versions of each file in the default
     directory.
